From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jxlarrea <jx@jxl.me>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:18:30 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] misc: Add the Echo Dot's ambient light sensor drivers

The Echo Dot (2nd gen) carries a TSL2584TSV or a TSL2540, and its device
tree declares both. These are Amazon's drivers from the Fire OS 6.5.7.1
Biscuit kernel, which this kernel lacked, so the light sensor HAL found
nothing:

- tsl2583 for the TSL2584TSV, an IIO device with the factory
  calibration from IDME's alscal.
- ams_tsl2540 with its ALS part and ams_i2c, which publish the lux on
  the I2C device's sysfs.

Port to 4.9: the raw channel and calibrated lux attributes take a
writable buffer, and tsl2583 suspends and resumes through dev_pm_ops,
since i2c_driver lost its own hooks. biscuit_defconfig turns both on
with the options Fire OS 6 used.
---
 arch/arm64/configs/biscuit_defconfig |    5 +
 drivers/misc/Kconfig                 |   44 +
 drivers/misc/Makefile                |    2 +
 drivers/misc/ams_i2c.c               |  201 ++++
 drivers/misc/ams_i2c.h               |   44 +
 drivers/misc/ams_tsl2540.c           |  980 ++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/misc/ams_tsl2540_als.c       |  946 +++++++++++++++++
 drivers/misc/ams_tsl2540_als.h       |   29 +
 drivers/misc/tsl2583.c               | 1441 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/i2c/ams_tsl2540.h      |  266 +++++
 10 files changed, 3958 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/ams_i2c.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/ams_i2c.h
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/ams_tsl2540.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/ams_tsl2540_als.c
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/ams_tsl2540_als.h
 create mode 100644 drivers/misc/tsl2583.c
 create mode 100644 include/linux/i2c/ams_tsl2540.h

